    "result_text": "All 272 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners, following the existing derived-field pattern in this OpenAPI-generated Spring Boot app.\n\nThe value must persist (owners are read back later via `GET`, and each new owner shifts the count), so I stored it on the entity rather than computing it at read time:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` (integer, `int32`) property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 assign `owner.setMembershipNumber(clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1)` before saving, so each owner gets one more than the count of owners that existed before it.\n4. **schema.sql** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column (ddl-auto is `none`, so the SQL schema is authoritative; tests run on hsqldb).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps `Owner.membershipNumber \u2192 OwnerDto.membershipNumber`, so no mapper change was needed. The `Cp09Tests` invariant (two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) passes, along with the full suite.",
